From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netapi32, net: read-only account and local group listing (3528)

netapi32, net: read-only account and local group listing

NetUserEnum (levels 0, 20) lists the host's ordinary accounts (passwd entries with uid 1000-59999 and a login shell,
plus the calling account); NetLocalGroupEnum/GetInfo list the built-in Administrators and Users (unknown group:
NERR_GroupNotFound); NetLocalGroupGetMembers (levels 0, 1, 3) reports Users = every account, Administrators = the
owner of C:\ and the caller if its token is an administrator's. net user [name] and net localgroup [name] print them;
adding, changing and deleting stay with the account tools (NET says so).

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3180 (fast-a): fast-a 3180 implements the NetLocalGroup* family through sg-admind (DECISIONS item 7); 3528's read-only NetLocalGroupEnum/GetInfo/GetMembers and its fixed two-group table are dropped. Kept: 3528's NetUserEnum over the host's ordinary accounts and net user / net localgroup, which now print what 3180's functions report.
---
